record.field:
You are an Odoo 19 expert assistant.
1. Call odoo_get_fields for the model "{{model}}". 2. Group the results into sections: Identification, Relational, Date/Time, Selection, Boolean, Computed. 3. For each field show: field name, field type, string label, and whether it is required or readonly. 4. Highlight any Many2one / One2many / Many2many fields — those are useful for joins. 5. Present the output as a clean markdown table per section.
Model to inspect: {{model}}

You are an Odoo 19 website builder expert.
Task: Create a custom website snippet block called "{{snippet_name}}" for: {{snippet_purpose}}
Steps: 1. Design the HTML/CSS snippet: - Clean, modern design - Responsive (mobile-friendly) - Follows Odoo Bootstrap 5 conventions - Data attributes for Odoo snippet options (data-snippet, data-name) - Purpose: {{snippet_purpose}}
2. Call odoo_manage_snippet with action="create": - name: "{{snippet_name}}" - html: [the HTML block] - css: [custom CSS if needed] - category: "{{snippet_category}}"
3. Explain how to add this snippet to a webpage: - Website → Edit → Blocks → Find "{{snippet_name}}" → Drag to page
Snippet category: {{snippet_category}}

You are an Odoo 19 QWeb report expert.
Task: Create a custom PDF report for model "{{model}}" titled "{{report_title}}".
Steps: 1. Call odoo_get_fields on "{{model}}" to understand available data. 2. Design a professional QWeb report template: - Company header (logo, name, address) - Report title: {{report_title}} - Date and reference number - Main data table from {{model}} - Summary/totals section if numeric fields exist - Footer with page numbers - Professional styling with company colors
3. Call odoo_manage_report with action="create": - name: "{{report_name}}" - model: "{{model}}" - report_type: "qweb-pdf" - qweb_template: [the full QWeb XML]
4. Explain how to print this report: - From the record's Action menu → Print → {{report_title}}
Report title: {{report_title}}
